Falsifies `file_allocation_table::time::verification::any_time_packs_to_legal_fields`.

The defect: a month of 13 is let through, so a clock that reports one writes a date no driver reads, and fsck refuses the volume.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(in_range)` after a successful pack.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/time.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/time.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/time.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/time.rs
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ impl Stamp {
         };
         let legal = now.year >= FIRST_YEAR
             && now.year <= LAST_YEAR
-            && (1..=12).contains(&now.month)
+            && (1..=13).contains(&now.month)
             && (1..=31).contains(&now.day)
             && now.hour <= 23
             && now.minute <= 59
